      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine which of the given functions have inverses. A function has an inverse if and only if it is a one-to-one function. A polynomial is one-to-one on any interval it is continuous on. Therefore, we need to check the continuity of each function.\n\nFunction A:\nThe graph of Function A is a cubic function with a single root at $x = 2$. Since it is not continuous at $x = 0$ (the root of the function) and has a vertical asymptote at $x = 0$, it is not one-to-one. Therefore, Function A does not have an inverse.\n\nFunction B:\nThe graph of Function B is a parabola with a single peak and a vertical asymptote at $x = 0$. Since it is not continuous at $x = 0$ and has a discontinuity at the peak, it is not one-to-one. Therefore, Function B does not have an inverse.\n\nFunction C:\nThe graph of Function C is a straight line with a slope greater than 1, starting at the point $(0, -3)$. Since it is continuous and has no breaks, it is one-to-one. Therefore, Function C has an inverse.\n\nFunction D:\nThe graph of Function D is a semicircle with a radius of 4 centered at the origin, and a circular arc with a radius of 4 centered at $(2, 0)$, with a tangent at $x = 2$ equal to half the length of the radius. Since it is continuous and has no breaks, it is one-to-one. Therefore, Function D has an inverse.\n\nFunction E:\nThe graph of Function E is a cubic function with a positive leading coefficient, starting at the origin. Since it is not continuous at $x = -5$ and has a vertical asymptote at $x = -5$, it is not one-to-one. Therefore, Function E does not have an inverse.\nThe function inverses are $C, D$.\nThe answer is C,D",
